[?1049h[>4;2m[?1h=[?2004h[?1004h[1;24r[?12h[?12l[22;2t[22;1t[27m[23m[29m[m[H[2J[?25l[24;1H"README.md" 257L, 26428B[2;1H▽[6n[2;1H  [3;1HPzz\[0%m[6n[3;1H           [1;1H[>c[1;1H# AI Session Tracker[2;1H[K[3;1HA zero-dependency, local web dashboard that shows you **what your AI coding sesss[4;1Hions are doing —[4;18Hlive**, across tools. It reads the session logs each AI coding  [5;1Htool already writes to disk and turns them into one readable view: a plain-languu[6;1Hage summary, todos, files touched, commands run, background agents/shells, and tt[7;1Hhe assistant's own narration —[7;32Hrefreshing every 2 seconds.

Works across tools via a small **provider** for each. Built in today: **Claude CC[10;1Hode** and **Auggie / Augment**. Adding another is a ~2-function adapter (see [Add[11;1Hding a tool](#adding-a-tool)).

Nothing is sent anywhere. It's a single Python file using only the standard librr[14;1Hary, serving a local page you open in your browser.

